#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:74
#: d000a890dd604b83bfe03d91cb6ac98a
msgid "Dshot capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:76
#: 1814be7b8d55467aac2fa4e6823b83db
msgid "All motor/servo outputs are Dshot and PWM capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs. The output groups that must be the same (PWM rate or Dshot, when configured as a normal servo/motor output) are: 1/2, 3/4, 5/6, 7/8/9 , and 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:78
#: ebacb70b3686466382f8867e2a3fa1bf
msgid "PWM9 is a solder pad, and PWM10 is marked as \"LED\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:81
#: a3c44e46106e4babbd07b5818a6bf37e
msgid "Outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:83
#: 637d23ea74514e698668e72034624270
msgid "The first 8 servo/motor outputs are marked on the board: M1,M2,S3-S8 . S9 is a solder pad on the board, and S10 is connected to the pin marked LED in ArduPilot's definition. Using S10 allows the easy grouping for odd numbers of motors with a common DShot or PWM frequency without sacrificing the use of an output for servo use due to rate issues (see above Dshot discussion)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:87
#: cc45b34447404a358f5f92bfdc363a2d
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:89
#: 5153a24108d8467ea838a200562ffb64
msgid "The SBUS pin, is passed by an inverter to R2 (UART2 RX), which by default is mapped to a timer input instead of the UART, and can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:91
#: 38a4e85f3b154276b71aa602a1bccf0d
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the R2 pin can also be configured to be used as true UART2 RX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to “1” so it becomes the SERIAL7 port's RX input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:93
#: bb8d90a169104d09936cc6db21b3cb8f
msgid "With this option, :ref:`SERIAL7_PROTOCOL<SERIAL7_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:95
#: 7091cc958f4b482aaf920ba8cd561d5f
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:97
#: 3b8c25f586724e408e4c596f2bfd2a7d
msgid "DSM/SRXL connects to the R2  pin, but SBUS would still be connected to SBUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:99
#: 2d6bc8c3423f4a2098221dc6a2ce76eb
msgid "FPort requires connection to T2 and R2 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:101
#: e365f40892cc451c810d87fc14cbdbcf
msgid "CRSF also requires a T2 connection, in addition to R2, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:103
#: 9a125f85fbd4460b991b589a65f7ed18
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to T2 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405-wing.rst:105
#: 9a7fd011228f4db8b53c91fa0f330952
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

